const CORE_SECTIONS=[
{id:'introduction',title:'Introduction and scope of services',note:'The agreed applications and services.',body:`<p>Thank you for entrusting Turner Hopkins Services Limited, trading as Turner Hopkins Immigration Specialists, to assist with your immigration journey.</p><p>We will represent you in the immigration matters and applications listed in the scope of services below. This agreement is based on the information provided during our initial discussions and assessment.</p><p>If additional work becomes necessary, we will discuss the work and any change to the fees or terms with you before proceeding. Any agreed variation will be confirmed in writing.</p><p>To represent you effectively, please do not contact Immigration New Zealand or another government agency about the agreed applications without first discussing this with us. This helps maintain a consistent and accurate flow of information.</p><p>You may seek independent legal advice on this agreement and should ask us any questions before accepting it.</p>`},
{id:'professional',title:'Professional costs',note:'The professional fee and payment structure.',body:`<p>Our professional fees for the agreed immigration services are set out in the schedule below. The schedule has been prepared for this matter, taking account of the work involved and the expected stages of the process.</p><p>All professional fees are quoted in New Zealand dollars. The administration and disbursement charge and any applicable GST are set out in this agreement.</p>`},
{id:'government',title:'Government application costs',note:'Charges payable to the relevant agency.',body:`<p>The government application costs currently identified for the agreed pathway are listed below. These charges are generally paid directly to the relevant government agency when the application is submitted.</p><p>Government charges can change. We will confirm the applicable amount and payment method before each application is lodged.</p>`},
{id:'excluded',title:'What our fee does not include',note:'Third-party and external costs.',body:`<p>Our professional fees cover the advice, preparation and representation described in the agreed scope. They do not include third-party costs such as medical examinations, English-language tests, police certificates, translations, couriers, qualification assessments, registration charges or other external services unless the fee schedule expressly says otherwise.</p><p>These costs vary by provider and are normally paid directly by you. We will explain any external requirement relevant to the agreed applications.</p>`},
{id:'terms',title:'Terms of engagement',note:'Information accuracy, additional work and withdrawal.',body:`<p>Our agreement to act is based on the information provided to us. You must give complete and accurate information and promptly tell us about any change that may affect the work, including changes to family circumstances, employment, address, travel, health, character or immigration history.</p><p>The professional fee assumes that the agreed work can be completed within the expected service period shown in this agreement. If the matter is delayed, the scope changes or substantial additional work is required, we may charge for that work after discussing it with you.</p><p>Additional work is charged at the hourly rate shown in the template settings, taking account of professional fees already paid so that the same work is not charged twice.</p><p>If you withdraw or our engagement ends, we will compare the payments received with the work completed and issue an invoice or credit where appropriate. Refunds are uncommon because fees are generally charged as work is completed.</p>`},
{id:'service',title:'Service details',note:'Advisers and support-team involvement.',body:`<p>You may receive advice from more than one licensed immigration adviser within Turner Hopkins Services Limited so that service can continue if an adviser is unavailable. Where practical, we will tell you if responsibility for the matter changes.</p><p>You may also deal with members of our support team. Support staff can collect information, arrange documents and assist with administration, but they do not provide immigration advice.</p>`},
{id:'important',title:'Important information',note:'Professional standards and regulatory documents.',body:`<p>Licensed immigration advisers are required to meet professional and ethical standards. You can access and review the <a href="https://www.iaa.govt.nz/assets/documents/tools/code-conduct-2014.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Code of Conduct</a> directly through this link. If you cannot open the document, please tell us and we will send you a copy.</p><p>By accepting this agreement, you acknowledge that the Code of Conduct and relevant professional standards information have been made available to you, and that you have had an opportunity to review them and ask questions.</p>`},
{id:'complaints',title:'Complaints policy and feedback',note:'How concerns are raised and resolved.',body:`<p>We aim to provide accurate, timely and professional service. If you have a concern, please raise it in writing with your adviser so that we can address it promptly and practically.</p><p>Where no further information is required, we aim to respond within 10 working days. If the issue requires more investigation, we will update you on progress and the expected timeframe.</p><p>If you remain dissatisfied and the complaint is eligible, you may refer it to the Registrar of Immigration Advisers. The agreement will contain the current contact details and information about the relevant complaints process.</p>`},
{id:'referrals',title:'Referral services',note:'Third-party referrals and consent.',body:`<p>We may be able to introduce you to other service providers relevant to your immigration or relocation process. In limited cases, Turner Hopkins may receive a referral fee if you choose to engage a provider.</p><p>We will not provide your personal information to a third party without your consent. Tell us if you do not wish to receive referrals or third-party recommendations.</p>`},
{id:'commitment',title:'Our commitment and service standards',note:'The service standards we aim to meet.',body:`<p>Our commitment is to provide accurate and timely advice and to assist you through the agreed immigration process.</p><ul><li>Provide clear instructions for each stage of the process.</li><li>Respond to questions within one business day where reasonably possible.</li><li>Communicate professionally and respectfully.</li><li>Build a relationship based on trust, credibility and honest advice.</li></ul><p>If you believe we have not met these standards, tell us as early as possible so the issue can be addressed while the work continues.</p>`},
{id:'authorisation',title:'Authorisation and acceptance',note:'Client confirmation of the agreement.',body:`<p>To retain our services, each required signatory must accept this agreement and confirm the professional fees, government costs and payment terms.</p><p>The final CRM process will provide a secure review-and-acceptance link and preserve the exact agreement version accepted by each signatory.</p>`},
{id:'payment',title:'Payment',note:'Invoices, payment methods and overdue accounts.',body:`<p>Once the agreement has been accepted, we will begin the work required for the first agreed stage and issue the relevant invoice.</p><p>Payment can be made by direct credit or by secure credit-card payment using the invoice details provided by our accounts team. We do not store or retain credit-card details.</p><p>Unless otherwise agreed, overdue invoices may attract interest at the rate shown in this agreement. Unpaid amounts may be referred for recovery, and the reasonable costs of recovery may be added where the agreement and applicable law permit.</p>`},
{id:'remember',title:'Remember THiS',note:'Closing and contact wording.',body:`<p>We are here to assist you. If you have questions about this agreement or the immigration process discussed with you, please contact us before accepting the agreement.</p><p>We look forward to working closely with you to achieve your immigration objectives.</p>`}
];
